BIGVIC 2 was developed to convert pc graphics into c64 graphics.

It works with a resolution of 320 x 200 pixels (or less) in 256 colors and
the pcx or lbm (both, iff or pbx) format. So you have to convert your graphics
to one of these formats first using eg photoshop 4.0.

You are now able to load your graphic into BIGVIC and convert them in one of
the nine c64 formats supported. For a short example, just load X-AMPLE.PCX,
enter any filename and format you like, press 'L' to load the colorsettings
and select X-AMPLE.BVP. Now you are able to see the result of the picture
by pressing 'F3'. It is a interlaced FLI-Picture, you might know from our
promotional slideshow SPACE BUBBLES 2 for the c64.

BIGVIC 2 supports the following c64 formats:

	Bitmap		pure bitmap without any color information.
			uses a percentual dithermethod when dithermode is
			activated.

	OCP		OCP Art Studio. A hires format, with color
			information.

	HIFLI		Hires FLI format with 8 videorams, one for each
			cursorline.

	KOALA		standard multicolor format, with one color- and
			one videoram. Could be dithered for better results.

	MCI		Multicolor Interlaced, with two bitmaps, two video-,
			but one colorram.

	KOALA INT.	Koala Interlace. Pretty the same as above, but with
			two colorrams.

	FLI		FLI format with 8 videorams.

	IFLI		Interlaced FLI format, eg. fun- or gunpaint.
			Two bitmaps, 16 videorams, one colorram.

	FLINT		FLI Interlace with 2 colorrams for even better
			results.

For further information about the functions of BIGVIC 2, check out the help-
page in the program. Simply press 'F1', when in editing mode.

To order your personal copy of BIGVIC 2 with saving enabled, just email us at
